+# Private G5 exporter implementation proposal
+
+This proposal does not authorize graph conversion, weight reads, native/GPU execution, or qualification. Root must first accept the actual FP32 gate and land the new native G5 math/provider authority. The module has no executable entry point. Original source graphs and external files remain immutable; exports create a new directory and fail closed, retaining partial output on error.
+
+## Sources and tensors
+
+Only the authenticated original full-FP32 Focus static512 graph (19b20ad4...), Compact c79c6725..., and Large f8ba5d3e... are accepted. Focus W8 and failed GQA/Dense candidates are rejected. Context publisher checkpoints are BF16, losslessly expanded to FP32 by the authenticated original exporter; this is not publisher FP32 storage. Conversion starts from those authenticated logical FP32 arrays and must later be checked against an independent publisher decode. Every source external file requires an exact SHA/size pin. All initializers are counted and classified; unknown weights, biases, quantization, aliases/overlapping external ranges, functions, graph mutations and unexpected topology refuse. Norm scale weights and Focus two-row head remain FP32. All embeddings and seven learned projections per layer become binary16, round-to-nearest-even, with no clipping. NaN/Inf and finite overflow refuse. Every range and converted output is digested. Original small Constant tensor data are retained FP32, including the static Focus mask.
+
+## Math boundaries and ABI
+
+Projection/embedding storage and GEMM outputs are half. Casts restore FP32 before original residual, RMSNorm, Q/K norm, RoPE, SiLU, multiplication and readout nodes. Context candidate rows come from the SAME rounded half embedding and only the gathered rows become FP32; no full FP32 embedding duplicate. Focus original two-row FP32 head and both output logits remain exact. The external three-input Focus and six-input Context native ABIs and output declarations remain unchanged. Native compiler input validation remains mandatory; this graph does not invent a second compiler.
+
+Replace only the reviewed original causal attention chains. Context uses half GroupQueryAttention, source scale bits, causal=1, do_rotary=0, no bias/cache and current all-live sequential positions. Focus repeats each KV head consecutively, uses half MultiHeadAttention causal=1, no bias/cache and packed mask [live,pad,512,pad,512]. Native Focus input remains a nonempty left-padded suffix with position_ids=0..511. Where replaces undefined padded query outputs with half zero BEFORE output projection/residual; multiplication by zero is forbidden. Whole reachable source causal masks disappear only because no consumer remains. Every retained source node is byte-identical except classified learned-weight consumers. Unknown attention topology refuses.
+
+## Runtime and acceptance remain held
+
+sdpa_kernel is a CUDA provider option, NOT an ONNX attribute. Native G5 must bind Context Flash-only=1 or Focus MEA-only=2, ORT_CUDA_GEMM_OPTIONS=2 before singleton creation, TF32 off, compute32F, and no reduced-precision reduction. SM86 only for this scientific path. Actual node/dtype/kernel observations must prove Flash or MEA; flags alone prove nothing. No within-call fallback or old profile retagging. New graph/profile/compiler/math identities and full external-data/ABI native admission are required.
+
+Frozen limits remain matching raw<=.001, matching mass Focus<=.00001/Context<=.05, original-FP32 raw Focus<=.25/Context<=.001, original mass<=.05, finite and identical argmax. Independent Torch original and half recipes, full native tensor provenance, genuine process settlement, numerical/resources/placement and full Answer latency gates remain required. Literal controls qualify only exporter mechanics, never selected models or GPU execution.
+
+The selected original graphs have no learned projection bias. Unexpected learned bias refuses rather than silently converting an unreviewed add/broadcast boundary. The implementation does not expose a command that bypasses the existing native admission owner. export_after_owner_admission is a library API for a future reviewed owner, not evidence that such admission currently exists. Original source closure authentication precedes conversion and is repeated afterward; the caller owns the immutable input/process/identity fence and the single absolute deadline.
