+# G5 full-half exporter: private implementation proposal
+
+No selected graph was transformed, no selected external weights were read or converted, and no Torch/ORT session, GPU, native model or Cargo process ran. This is actual exporter code plus synthetic mechanical evidence, not G5 qualification.
+
+`export_half.py` has no CLI. A future reviewed native/export owner invokes `export_after_owner_admission` only after the genuine first FP32 gate passes and new G5 math/admission policy exists. The caller owns same-human identity, immutable source/process/descriptor custody, existing original compiler tensors, native input validation, output policy and one absolute deadline. This module does not create an admission receipt or mirror native DTOs.
+
+The API accepts only original full-FP32 protobuf SHAs and exact original external closure pins. Focus starts from original static512 export19b20ad4, never the shipped W8 graph5072. Compact starts c79c and Large f8ba. Context publisher files are BF16 expanded losslessly by the authenticated original exporter. Both half recipes must be independently compared with those publisher logical arrays; no actual publisher/graph-weight equality was re-established by these synthetic tests.
+
+Implementation: complete learned weight census; finite IEEE754 binary16 conversion in bounded4MiB chunks; FP32 norm scales/Focus two-row head; explicit half GEMM and embedding boundaries around retained FP32 math; same rounded Context embedding for sparse readout; source-scale exact-bit causal half GQA or packed-mask MHA; Where-zero undefined padded Focus queries. No learned bias exists in selected originals; unknown bias refuses. Protected original nodes/ABIs retain bytes. Outputs are create-new and partial failure artifacts remain truthful. Source external files are fully authenticated before and after conversion; all converted ranges have separate source/output digests.
+
